An F2 individual necessarily carries a pair drawn from this set. Because the identical directional rule governs the second meiosis, its single crossover can regenerate only another member of the same four-element set; reversal, cancellation or extra transitions remain mechanically impossible. Consequently the F3 chromosome pool contains precisely those four sequences.

